<header><p class="st-kicker">margraviate · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Margraviate of Hachberg</h1><p class="st-meta">1190 CE – 1503 CE (approx.) · capital Emmendingen</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Breisgau branch of the margraves of Baden, named after the Hachberg castle and later holding Rötteln, Sausenberg and Neuchâtel before reuniting with Baden in 1503.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 1190 the lands of Margrave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hermann-iv-margrave-of-baden">Hermann IV of Baden</a> were divided, and his son Henry received the castle of Hachberg, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hochburg">Hochburg</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emmendingen">Emmendingen</a>, with lands in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/breisgau">Breisgau</a>. Henry and his heirs styled themselves margraves of Hachberg, founding a separate branch of the house of Zähringen-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden">Baden</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The margraves held scattered lordships in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/breisgau">Breisgau</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/markgraflerland">Markgräflerland</a>. In 1306 the house split into Hachberg proper and Hachberg-Sausenberg, which gained <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rotteln-castle">Rötteln</a> in 1315 and, through marriage, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-neuchatel">County of Neuchâtel</a> in the 15th century. Hachberg proper was sold back to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden">Baden</a> in 1415. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-of-hachberg-sausenberg">Philip of Hachberg-Sausenberg</a> served the dukes of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-burgundy">Burgundy</a> and the French crown.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Philip died in 1503 without a son, and under an inheritance treaty his lands returned to the margraves of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden">Baden</a>, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neuchatel">Neuchâtel</a> passed through his daughter to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-orleans-longueville">Orléans-Longueville</a> family. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/markgraflerland">Markgräflerland</a> name recalls their rule.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="margraviate, 1190 CE – 1503 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">margraviate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:83.38%;width:6.23%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1190 CE – 1503 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>margraviate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Emmendingen</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Henry I of Hachberg, Rudolf IV of Hachberg-Sausenberg, Philip of Hachberg-Sausenberg</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Alemannic German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Hachberg, Hochberg, Hachberg-Sausenberg</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1346&amp;focus=margraviate-of-hachberg" aria-label="Margraviate of Hachberg on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4863 494 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Margraviate of Hachberg lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5183 750L5191 731"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5191 731h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5183 750h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5183 750h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Emmendingen. <a href="/atlas?year=1346&amp;focus=margraviate-of-hachberg">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></